Drop hermetic-llvm's `-rtlib=compiler-rt` link arg on macOS.

rules_rust forwards the cc_toolchain's link args to rustc, and rustc links
Apple targets with `-nodefaultlibs`, so clang never selects a runtime library
and warns `argument unused during compilation: '-rtlib=compiler-rt'`. rustc's
`linker_messages` lint then prints that on every darwin Rust link. compiler-rt
is the clang driver's only runtime library on Darwin, so omitting the flag
there leaves C++ links unchanged.

Re-check on every `llvm` bump: the `rtlib` cc_args_list in
`toolchain/BUILD.bazel` (and `rtlib_compiler_rt` in `toolchain/args/BUILD.bazel`).
Drop once hermetic-llvm stops passing `-rtlib` on macOS; without this patch
the `-rtlib=compiler-rt` linker_messages warning returns on
`bazel build //src/cli/rust:sipi`.

--- a/toolchain/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/toolchain/BUILD.bazel
@@ -264,9 +264,10 @@
 # and paths when resolving compiler runtime libraries from the resource-dir.
 cc_args_list(
     name = "rtlib",
-    args = [
-        "//toolchain/args:rtlib_compiler_rt",
-    ],
+    args = select({
+        "@platforms//os:macos": [],
+        "//conditions:default": ["//toolchain/args:rtlib_compiler_rt"],
+    }),
 )

 cc_args_list(
